1
00:00:00,269 --> 00:00:02,859
(Penny:)I love San Francisco.
I wish I was going with you.

2
00:00:03,022 --> 00:00:04,232
(Sheldon:)I understand your envy.

3
00:00:04,398 --> 00:00:06,438
(Sheldon:)This is a can't-miss symposium.

4
00:00:06,609 --> 00:00:10,239
(Sheldon:)There are going to be discussions
on bioorganic cellular computer devices...

5
00:00:10,404 --> 00:00:12,824
(Sheldon:)...advancements
in multi-threaded task completion...

6
00:00:12,990 --> 00:00:16,660
...plus a round table on the non-equilibrium
Green's Function approach...

7
00:00:16,827 --> 00:00:19,037
(Sheldon:)...to the photoionization process
in atoms.

8
00:00:20,164 --> 00:00:23,794
(Penny:)When I go, I usually just get hammered
and ride the cable cars.

9
00:00:24,168 --> 00:00:25,838
This conference is a big thing.

10
00:00:26,003 --> 00:00:28,383
(Leonard:)The keynote address
is delivered by George Smoot.

11
00:00:28,839 --> 00:00:30,719
(Penny:)Oh, my God. The George Smoot?

12
00:00:30,883 --> 00:00:33,723
- You've heard of him?
- Of course I haven't.

13
00:00:34,929 --> 00:00:37,599
(Leonard:)George Smoot
is a Nobel Prize-winning physicist...

14
00:00:37,765 --> 00:00:39,645
(Sheldon:)...one of the great minds of our time.

15
00:00:39,809 --> 00:00:41,349
(Sheldon:)His work in black body form...

16
00:00:41,519 --> 00:00:44,519
(Sheldon:)...and anisotropy of the cosmic
microwave background radiation...

17
00:00:44,688 --> 00:00:47,978
(Sheldon:)...cemented our understanding
of the origin of the universe.

18
00:00:48,150 --> 00:00:49,860
(Penny:)It's kind of a funny name though.

19
00:00:50,027 --> 00:00:52,027
(Leonard:)Smoot.

20
00:00:54,865 --> 00:00:56,495
(Sheldon:)It's like talking to a chimp.

21
00:00:58,119 --> 00:01:01,249
(Penny:)Okay, now that I've been completely
insulted, have a good flight.

22
00:01:01,413 --> 00:01:04,543
- Yeah, I wish.
- We're not flying. We're taking the train.

23
00:01:04,708 --> 00:01:05,788
(Penny:)Oh, cool.

24
00:01:05,960 --> 00:01:10,670
(Howard:)Yeah, cool. Seven times as long as flying
and costs almost twice as much.

25
00:01:12,049 --> 00:01:14,509
- Well then why are you doing it?
- Well, we had a vote.

26
00:01:14,677 --> 00:01:17,097
Three voted for airplane,
Sheldon voted for train.

27
00:01:17,263 --> 00:01:19,723
(Leonard:)So we're taking the train.

28
00:01:20,558 --> 00:01:27,028
Don't say it like that, Leonard.
Say it like, "We're taking the train!"

